// The Library: works, levelled passages and "lines of the hour".
//
// Rules this file keeps (docs/00-spec.md §3, §4, §7):
// - Only public-domain texts are held in full (app/public/texts/<id>.txt, fetched by
//   tools/texts/fetch.mjs from the GITenberg mirror of Project Gutenberg).
// - Modern works are cards only: title, author, our own summary, why it matters. Never quoted.
// - Every LINE is an exact substring of its held text; test/texts.mjs fails any that is not.
// - Passages are originals (abridged: false). Their text is cut from the held file by
//   tools/texts/levels.mjs, from `start` to `end` inclusive, into passages.json.
// - Period attitudes are never silently cut. A passage or work that carries one is marked
//   needsReview: true with a note for the grown-up, until a named reviewer clears it.
//
// Rights are as of `checked`. US: published 1930 or earlier. UK/EU: author (and translator)
// died 1955 or earlier (70 years). India: died 1965 or earlier (60 years).

